  "notes": [
    "Amounts are monthly KRW. No measured usage, payment settlement or real external generation.",
    "FX1600 and 20% AI buffer are budgeting assumptions, not spot FX or a guarantee. No cache/batch savings assumed.",
    "Prices VAT-inclusive; fee rate3.85% of gross is a conservative web-payment assumption, not an agreed PSP quote. Alternate platform percentages here are stress tests on the same gross-fee basis, not official Apple settlement calculations.",
    "Free ratio3:1, 300 KRW/free user, paid data/index reserve200, normal support1k/heavy3k, replacement marketing1500 are assumptions. Extra acquisition spend, corporate tax, unknown compliance quotes and headcount beyond one 3M labor allowance are excluded.",
    "Infrastructure200k and operating risk50k are planning reserves, not capacity-tested provider quotations. 500-paid-user rows retain the same fixed reserve for comparability and need additional capacity/infra stress before launch.",
    "AI cap4k/18k and workload routing are proposals. Existing production has an absolute4k cap and25% funding rule. It has not been increased or funded. Pricing is not enforcement.",
    "Standard document uses aggregate60k/12k tokens across3 steps. Complex document uses aggregate600k/30k plus5 searches and1GB20min container. These are workload estimates, not output guarantees.",
    "Source batching, change-only generation and mini/nano routing are assumed. Actual provider model configuration, source permissions, tool caps, result quality and per-request reservations must be measured.",
    "Shared AI allowance includes briefing, analysis, drafting, chat, tools, failures and repeated work. A per-call cap, concurrent pre-reservation and server stop are necessary."
  ]
